00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:56.960
Pannier mau daikaiten

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:58.710
Maid kissa de kakurenbo

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:00.420
Nice okyuuji daiseikyou

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.210
Renai wa no no

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:04.540
Himitsu no hanazono

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:09.330
One Miracle Pork Stew meal, anypig else?

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:09.330
To Die for Love:

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:09.330
Tears Fall on Electric Town

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.130
Hamks for the song request!

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:12.960
Here we go, in full swineg!

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:15.040
"The Pure Maid's Killer Kiss!"

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:20.630
Kimi ni girari moe kyun! Moe bakyun
I'm targeting you, moe kyun! Moe and blam!

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:20.170
The Lady Omoe effect is crazy; we're raking it in.

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:22.630
A shot of caffeine into my master.

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:24.750
Your Pearls Before Swine Coffee, oink.

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:26.830
Thank you.

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:30.380
Himitsu no tobira akete
Open the secret door

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:32.000
Is something wrong?

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:32.000
Ai ni kite goshujinsama
And come see me, Master

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:37.710
No, I just thought it foolish to assume that pigs
wouldn't understand the value of pearls.

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:40.790
I must say I don't understand, myself.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:42.500
I'm sorry.

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:45.080
But I think pearls would suit you, Miss Ranko.

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.630
It looks like they're hitting it off.

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:51.580
Oh, that person after Ranko?

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:53.880
Don't you think they're quite a match?

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:55.250
What are you saying?!

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:56.460
Come on, everyone!

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:58.250
We need to make the most of this chance we've got!

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:01.080
But doesn't Ranko kinda sorta look interested, too?

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.080
Romance between a master and a maid is off limits!

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:06.040
If she breaks the group rules...

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:07.330
They'll disown her.

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.920
She wouldn't get out of Akiba alive, that's for sure.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:12.000
But I betcha Ranko could evade 'em.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.790
No I mean, it's all over once a maid falls in love.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:16.420
Ranko is a maid!

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.250
Maids don't fall in love!

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:20.210
Ranko!

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:22.040
Was it a riveting conversation?

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:24.250
Do you mean with Mr. Suehiro?

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:26.000
Aw, you remember his name.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.000
I learned it.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.210
What did you talk about?

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:31.710
He asked me if I wanted to go out
somewhere with him this weekend.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:32.710
Whaaat?!

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:33.210
A date!

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:33.880
For real?
A date!

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.250
And you said yes?!

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:37.250
No, I have yet to reply.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:41.630
Ranko, Saturday at eleven o'clock.
You're meeting in front of the station.

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:43.380
You just went and said yes?!

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:45.420
C'mon, he's a banker.

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:48.580
Just lead him on a bit and
he'll lend us loads of money!

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:49.580
Is that true?

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:53.130
Well, only a banker would carry around
an attaché case like that.

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:54.500
You can't be serious.

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:58.040
I set things up nicely,
so you go have a word with him, Ranko.

00:03:58.040 --> 00:03:59.380
He's just about to leave.

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:00.710
Go ahead.

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:05.250
Chief, this isn't allowed!

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:09.330
It's just a little date.
All the cafes do it, it's fine!

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:13.290
We eagerly await your return.

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:21.130
Ranko, are you looking forward to it?

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:22.380
What do you mean?

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:25.210
What? I mean the date, of course.

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:28.500
Perhaps I am looking forward to it.

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:30.500
I'm sorry.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:33.420
I should be rooting for your happiness.

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:34.880
No.

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:39.830
The idea of finding happiness is something
I cast aside when I entered the maid business.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:42.420
A maid cannot hope for that kind of thing.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:47.500
But I've definitely had moments of happiness
getting to be a maid with you, Ranko!

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:48.710
You're too kind.

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:52.460
Um! Let me help you out with your date, Ranko.

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:55.420
Do you have experience going on dates, Nagomi?

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:56.630
Of course I do!

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:00.420
Actually I don't, I lied.

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:04.710
Oinky Doink Cafe

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:12.500
Good morning.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:14.250
Is something wrong?

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:17.960
I apologize.

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:20.000
I must go out today.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:30.210
Good morning!

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:30.710
Good morning.

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:31.960
Come over here a moment!
Good morning.

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:33.960
Get it, though?

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:36.250
A real woman never takes her wallet out.

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:38.880
That's how you become a woman of high value.

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:40.580
It's what I've always done.

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:43.670
Gotta feel good about how you look on a date, y'know?

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:46.040
It's a date, after all. Right?

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:49.170
This is a dress I got from my babushka!

00:05:51.670 --> 00:05:53.540
Wow, you look mad nice.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.540
S-so pretty!

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:57.960
You're not bad-looking to begin with, after all.

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:00.420
And they won't recognize your mug this way.

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:01.880
Listen, Ranko.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:04.710
I think maids deserve to find happiness, too!

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:07.380
Thank you.

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:09.750
Go enjoy yourself today!

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:13.250
I shall go about it with dogged determination.

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:21.750
Please excuse me.

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:27.040
Go on ahead.

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:31.250
Wh...

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:33.790
What do you think happiness-

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:48.380
Have you been waiting long?

00:06:48.790 --> 00:06:50.000
No.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:51.210
Shall we?

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:56.000
That suits you very well.

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:02.000
11:30 ~ Strolling around Ueno ~ Browsing the Ameyoko Street Market

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:09.000
Into the bag, into the bag, we throw in extra!

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:11.330
Hey, missus! How 'bout one for dinner tonight?!

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:19.630
13:00 ~ Eating Ranko's Bento at Ueno Park

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:23.880
Did you make this, Miss Ranko?

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:25.210
I'm afraid so.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:28.670
That way you talk...

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:31.170
It was surprising to hear the first time.

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:32.880
I apologize,

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:34.830
I only know how to speak in this stiff manner.

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:37.420
Oh no, I really like the way you talk.

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:54.920
14:00 ~ Seeing the Animals at Ueno Zoo

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:33.330
Your first

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:33.330
apartment?

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:33.330
Huge sale on heaters

00:08:32.330 --> 00:08:34.080
Do you like fan heaters?

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:39.420
Yes, I do.

00:08:39.630 --> 00:08:41.420
They're great, huh? Fan heaters?

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:46.420
I have one in my place too,
but I don't feel like I get warm at all recently.

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:48.580
Perhaps it might be broken?

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:51.040
That may be it.

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:53.040
What if we buy a kotatsu?

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:55.790
We could make some hot pot and eat it at the kotatsu.

00:08:56.210 --> 00:08:59.330
That would be so warm,
I'm afraid we would fall asleep right there.

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:01.290
But that's the best part.

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:03.170
That does sound nice.

00:09:07.670 --> 00:09:10.040
Did I say something wrong?

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:11.040
No.

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:12.920
There's something wrong with me.

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:16.540
When I'm with you,
I let my guard down for some reason.

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:20.130
Miss Ranko...

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:22.920
Can we walk around for a little longer?

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:28.000
I was actually supposed to do a job today.

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:33.500
I've been fixated on work for so long,
I never took care of myself at all.

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:35.920
I thought that was what I had to do.

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:40.540
But that's when I met you, Miss Ranko.

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:42.210
Me?

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:48.880
I was worn out emotionally,
and you gave me a place of solace.

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:52.000
As long as I went to Oinky Doink Cafe,

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:56.460
I could forget about work and
the way you talked would cheer me up.

00:09:57.580 --> 00:09:59.960
With your frank but sincere attitude,

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:03.630
you had occupied a place in my heart
before I even knew it.

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:08.790
That's why I'm going to be
upfront and honest about this.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:13.460
Miss Ranko, would you consider
running away from Akiba together?

00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:17.290
I'm heading up north on the night train tomorrow.

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:19.830
I want you to make a decision by then.

00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:23.080
Obviously, I realize this is such a sudden proposition.

00:10:24.420 --> 00:10:25.710
I...

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:52.000
Tomorrow night at nine o'clock,
I'll be waiting at the station's Electric Town exit.

00:11:01.330 --> 00:11:03.500
LIMITED EXPRESS TICKET

00:11:01.330 --> 00:11:03.500
B Sleeper (Single Berth)

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:03.500
Ueno    to    Sapporo

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:03.500
(dep. 21:15)     (arr. 11:30)

00:11:06.460 --> 00:11:08.330
Did you want something from me?

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:14.040
Let me tell you...

00:11:14.830 --> 00:11:16.790
the story of a certain maid.

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:23.790
Once, there was a young girl who came to Akiba
with dreams of becoming a maid.

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:29.500
Although she got to be a maid,
all she was given was menial tasks.

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:35.630
But then, a master appeared who took a liking to her.

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:40.290
Her days as a maid had finally begun.

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:42.210
That was when...

00:11:43.630 --> 00:11:45.420
she was tasked with an important job.

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:49.880
She was supposed to perform a hit
on the head of a rival maid cafe.

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:56.210
Maid

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:56.210
Teahouse

00:11:53.830 --> 00:11:56.210
Exactly as some leaked information had suggested,

00:11:56.540 --> 00:12:00.000
the target's cafe was incredibly understaffed that day.

00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:07.080
And then, she pulled the trigger.

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:14.750
Chief!

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:23.380
In terror, the maid desperately told herself
that she would rise in the ranks now.

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:26.500
She finally had a master who favored her, too.

00:12:35.710 --> 00:12:37.960
But reality was harsh.

00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:40.580
His being a master was a lie.

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:43.130
The man had only approached

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:45.500
so he could eliminate me
once I had served my purpose.

00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:47.460
Is something the matter?

00:12:47.790 --> 00:12:49.500
Hey! What do you think you're doing?!

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:55.000
They never meant to make me a maid.

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:57.130
I was just disposable trash.

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:15.040
Panda Merch for Sale

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:16.960
Noodles are made in a pan, duh!

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:21.670
<i>Must be nice.</i>

00:13:21.880 --> 00:13:24.080
<i>I wish I could be a panda.</i>

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:27.380
And that's what led to this.

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:32.500
Do you know Ranko Mannen from Maid Teahouse?

00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:35.330
She got jailed for avenging her manager, right?

00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:39.750
O-meow-ko Club

00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:39.750
We'll grab you by the heart!

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:36.540
Scary stuff!

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:39.750
Safe for first-timers.

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:39.750
Hiring gyaru up to 21 y.o.

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:39.580
That cafe claimed it was anti-violence, the liars.

00:13:43.330 --> 00:13:45.670
Time moved forward without me.

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:45.830
Maid Teahouse

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:47.710
Akiba changed over the years...

00:13:45.830 --> 00:13:48.830
FOR LEASE

00:13:48.830 --> 00:13:50.130
Oinky Doink Cafe

00:13:56.670 --> 00:13:59.250
...and when the people of this town
had forgotten what had happened...

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:02.000
Permission to speak!

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:05.130
#96, Ranko Mannen, thirty-five years old.

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:08.000
...you appeared, Ranko,

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:12.000
right before me, the one who murdered
the manager of your cafe.

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:16.920
The only reason Suehiro approached you
is to kill you, Ranko.

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:19.420
Someone must have hired him to do it.

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:22.130
He may have given up today, but...

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:24.250
I can tell!

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:25.670
It's all a lie!

00:14:26.330 --> 00:14:29.170
All he cares about is eliminating his target.

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:32.880
That's why you can't go with him tomorrow.

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:35.420
If you do, he'll kill you in Hakodate or something.

00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:42.830
Ranko...

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:46.790
I'm sorry I took the life of someone
who was so dear to you.

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:51.790
I know that I should have told you sooner,
but I just couldn't.

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:01.750
I'm sorry I'm such a despicable pand-

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:12.460
Pl-please tell everyone that
I enjoyed my time with them.

00:15:14.210 --> 00:15:16.000
Allow me to send you off.

00:15:18.630 --> 00:15:21.040
Oinky Doink Cafe

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:21.130
Welcome back!

00:15:21.130 --> 00:15:22.330
You were out pretty late, huh?

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:22.960
How did it go?

00:15:22.960 --> 00:15:23.830
Did he just kiss you?!
How did it go?

00:15:23.830 --> 00:15:25.080
Didja see the panda?

00:15:25.290 --> 00:15:26.500
We did.

00:15:26.830 --> 00:15:29.130
I got to spend some incredibly precious time.

00:15:29.580 --> 00:15:33.250
I appreciate the arrangements
you all made for my sake.

00:15:33.380 --> 00:15:34.580
That's so great!

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:36.460
And that means the cafe's got it made now.

00:15:36.460 --> 00:15:39.580
You never know, this is only step one in a relationship.
Woooo! That's super duper sweet!

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:51.920
Allow me to send you off.

00:15:57.250 --> 00:16:01.580
I can't ever forgive you for killing Miss Michiyo.

00:16:01.580 --> 00:16:04.250
Then why aren't you killing me?

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:09.500
Because I think Miss Michiyo perhaps
wouldn't want that of me.

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:15.040
Ranko?

00:16:15.880 --> 00:16:17.380
Allow me to take care of him.

00:16:17.380 --> 00:16:18.380
But...

00:16:18.630 --> 00:16:20.880
He's my master, after all.

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:27.580
Could I interest you in this meal?

00:16:27.580 --> 00:16:30.500
Wow! Thanks, oinky doink!

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:39.040
Kuroishi Precious Metals

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:39.040
Metalworking Center

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:45.670
Thank you for letting me take a bath first!

00:16:50.170 --> 00:16:52.630
Mr. Suehiro didn't come today, did he?

00:16:53.460 --> 00:16:54.670
That's true.

00:16:57.580 --> 00:17:02.080
Seeing you and Mr. Suehiro together,
I think you make a lovely twosome!

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:07.380
To tell you the truth,
I was kind of scared of Mr. Suehiro at first.

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:12.830
But I think that was only because I was scared
that he would take you from us, Ranko.

00:17:13.420 --> 00:17:16.880
We almost got killed, drowned,
we played baseball, and even had to grovel...

00:17:17.540 --> 00:17:20.420
I got through all of that with you.

00:17:20.750 --> 00:17:22.920
If you leave, I'll definitely be sad.

00:17:23.130 --> 00:17:24.830
But please don't worry!

00:17:25.290 --> 00:17:27.830
In preparation for that time,

00:17:27.830 --> 00:17:32.250
I'll start practicing for your graduation now

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:35.420
so you can leave with a proper smile on your face.

00:17:35.750 --> 00:17:38.210
I promise I won't cry or anything!

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:42.540
But you're crying already.

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:45.170
Th-that's not true.

00:17:45.380 --> 00:17:47.130
I have you to thank, Nagomi.

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:49.880
If it weren't for you,

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:54.500
I never would have considered
what normal happiness might be like.

00:17:58.290 --> 00:17:59.500
I'm going.

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:00.710
Ranko?

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:08.750
Nagomi...

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:11.500
Please take care of Oinky Doink Cafe for me.

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:19.040
Ranko

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:39.540
I'll settle this my own way.

00:18:57.380 --> 00:19:00.080
Oh, I'm sorry, I made a mistake.

00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:01.080
Hey!

00:19:01.630 --> 00:19:02.960
What's the big idea?

00:19:02.960 --> 00:19:04.170
Uh, no no.

00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:25.130
What was that, an accident?

00:19:25.130 --> 00:19:26.670
That didn't sound good.

00:19:41.750 --> 00:19:42.960
Who are you?

00:19:43.540 --> 00:19:44.750
A panda.

00:19:46.630 --> 00:19:48.960
I see, a panda.

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:52.580
I can't let Ranko have to kill a master of hers.

00:20:04.080 --> 00:20:07.040
Why don't we chat for a bit?

00:20:15.330 --> 00:20:17.250
LIMITED EXPRESS TICKET

00:20:15.330 --> 00:20:17.250
B Sleeper (Single Berth)

00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:17.250
Ueno    to    Sapporo

00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:17.250
(dep. 21:15)     (arr. 11:30)

00:20:37.330 --> 00:20:39.290
Is this your idea of making amends?

00:20:41.330 --> 00:20:43.210
So you're back to being silent.

00:20:43.710 --> 00:20:45.960
Can I just tell you one thing?

00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:50.040
Fifteen years ago, the one who
had me kill Miss Michiyo

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:52.670
was the current head of Creatureland, Nagi.

00:20:53.670 --> 00:20:55.960
She gave the order this time, too.

00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:58.290
I see.

00:21:29.670 --> 00:21:34.580
Kyou mo ashita mo moe moe kyun

00:21:35.880 --> 00:21:40.960
Butagoya atari de moe moe kyun

00:21:41.830 --> 00:21:46.960
Sorega atai no ikizama sa

00:21:48.170 --> 00:21:56.790
Baka ni suru yatsa chi o miruze

00:21:56.790 --> 00:22:02.380
Mune o yogiru tamerai wa

00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:11.210
Hito no kokoro no nokoriga ka

00:22:11.830 --> 00:22:18.290
Ikirutomo haterutomo

00:22:18.540 --> 00:22:24.080
Onore no michi o tsuranuke

00:22:24.080 --> 00:22:30.460
Hikigane o hiki yagare

00:22:30.920 --> 00:22:36.830
Omae ga dare nanoka

00:22:37.040 --> 00:22:43.750
Itami de oshietokure

00:22:49.080 --> 00:22:50.290
What is it?

00:22:50.290 --> 00:22:52.080
I'm not going to kill Ranko Mannen.

00:22:52.420 --> 00:22:56.170
I thought I told you that crushing Oinky Doink Cafe
is what the group decided.

00:22:56.710 --> 00:23:02.540
Refusing to kill Ranko Mannen means defying
the Creatureland Group as a whole.

00:23:02.540 --> 00:23:04.420
Interpret it as you will.

00:23:04.630 --> 00:23:08.210
However you take it,
it's my mess so I'll settle this my own way.

00:23:08.460 --> 00:23:10.960
You intend to die with a pig for love?

00:23:10.960 --> 00:23:12.420
You have questionable taste.

00:23:12.580 --> 00:23:14.880
I don't need you to understand her value.
